This is an altered version of Echo's Z80 program.

prog-z80.bin is Echo 1.65 (github.com/sikthehedgehog/echo, commit e326c87,
built/prog-z80.bin) with two changes, both offered upstream:

1. The PSG frequency table (PSGFreqTable in src-z80/player/freq.z80, Z80
   address $1200-$128F) holds periods computed for the NTSC PSG clock
   (3579545 Hz) with A4 = 440 Hz, rounded to the nearest value. Echo's
   original table plays PSG notes 8 to 14 cents sharp in its lowest octave
   and up to 119 cents sharp at the top, and about 10 cents sharp of Echo's
   own FM notes. (sikthehedgehog/echo pull request 33.)

2. UpdatePSG (src-z80/player/psg.z80) keeps a PSG instrument's semitone
   shift inside the frequency table, holding the note at C-3 or B-8. The
   original reads past either end of the table and sends those bytes to the
   PSG, which can change another channel's volume or silence the noise
   channel. (sikthehedgehog/echo pull request 34.)

Built with z80asm 1.8 from Echo's source with both changes applied; the
unchanged source assembles to the original built/prog-z80.bin byte for byte.
The second change adds 11 bytes of code, taken from the padding before the
page-aligned tables, so code after it moves and the tables do not.

